# saan — system design

*saan* (Filipino for "where?") is a privacy-first, local file launcher. This
document describes the architecture as implemented in this repository. Every
claim below is grounded in the code; file paths are relative to the repo root.

## Components

| Component | Location | Responsibility |
|---|---|---|
| `saan-core` library | `crates/core/src` | Chunking, embedding, extraction, scope (multi-root walk with size cap), index, router, grep, glob, Jev client, engine. |
| `saan` CLI | `crates/cli/src/main.rs` | `fetch-model`, `index`, `search`, `grep`, `glob`, `eval`, `bench`; with **no subcommand** it launches the desktop app and exits. |
| Tauri app | `src-tauri/src/main.rs` | Desktop window + global hotkey, settings commands and persistence, background multi-folder indexing with progress/cancel, engine state, Jev wiring. |
| Frontend | `index.html`, `src/main.ts`, `src/style.css` | Plain TypeScript launcher UI (debounced search, keyboard nav, settings view with themes and folders, index progress, result metadata). |
| Installer | `scripts/install.ps1` | Builds the app with `npm run tauri build` (embeds the frontend) and the CLI with cargo. Stops any running launcher, copies both executables to `%LOCALAPPDATA%\saan\bin`, and copies or fetches the model to `%LOCALAPPDATA%\saan\models`. Puts `bin` on the user `PATH` through the raw registry value, so `%VAR%` entries and REG_EXPAND_SZ survive. `-Uninstall [-Purge]` reverses it. |

