### CLI commands (`crates/cli/src/main.rs`)

Global option: `--index <dir>` (default `$SAAN_INDEX_DIR` or `./.saan/index`).

| Command | Arguments | Behaviour |
|---|---|---|
| *(none)* | — | Launches the desktop app and exits 0. Calls `AllowSetForegroundWindow(ASFW_ANY)` so the launcher (or the running instance) can take focus from the terminal. Then spawns `saan-app[.exe]` found next to the running `saan.exe` (or `$SAAN_APP`) with `SAAN_SHOW=1`, detached on Windows (`DETACHED_PROCESS` + `CREATE_NEW_PROCESS_GROUP`) and with null stdio. Exits 1 with a clear message when the app binary is missing. |
| `fetch-model` | — | Downloads the files in `MODEL_FILES` from `MODEL_REPO` into `$SAAN_MODEL_DIR` or `./models/<MODEL_DIR_NAME>`, skipping files already present (`.part` temp file then rename). |
| `index <root>...` | `--max-file-mb <n>` (default 10) | Builds the index for one or more roots (`Scope::new(roots, n·1024·1024)`), reusing unchanged files when a previous index loads. Progress goes to stderr as `[done/total] eta 1m23s  rel` (at most one line per 250 ms); the stdout summary line is unchanged. |
| `search <query...>` | `-k <n>` (default 10), `--json` | Routed search; words are joined with spaces. Builds `Engine::new(index, model_dir, JevClient::from_env())`; the model loads on the first semantic use (grep/glob routes never load it). |
| `grep <pattern>` | `--root <dir>` (repeatable, default `.`), `--max-file-mb <n>` (default 10) | Direct regex search (no routing) over a `Scope` of the roots, prints `rel:line: text` (`GrepHit.rel` is the display rel). |
| `glob <pattern>` | `--root <dir>` (repeatable, default `.`), `--max-file-mb <n>` (default 10) | Direct glob search (no routing) over the same kind of `Scope`, prints `GlobHit.rel` per match. |
| `eval <file>` | `-k <n>` (default 5), `--min <rate>` (default 0.8) | Top-k hit rate over `{query, expected}` cases; exits failure below `--min`. Uses a **local-only** engine (`Engine::new(index, model_dir, None)`) so results are reproducible. |
| `bench <file>` | `--runs <n>` (default 5), `--max-ms <ms>` (default 100) | Warm p50/p95/max latency over the eval queries; exits failure if p95 ≥ `--max-ms`. Also local-only, and calls `Engine::preload()` before the warm-up loop so model load time is excluded from the measurement. |

`eval` and `bench` deliberately construct the engine with no `JevClient`, so Jev
is never consulted during measurement. Both resolve the model directory with
`find_model_dir()` and report the same "EmbeddingGemma not found" error as the
other commands when it is missing.

### Tauri commands (`src-tauri/src/main.rs`)

Commands take JSON arguments in camelCase (Tauri's default). The old
`index_folder` command is removed.

| Command | Signature | Behaviour |
|---|---|---|
| `search` | `(query: String, k: Option<usize>)` | `Engine::search`; `k` defaults to 12. Errors if no index is loaded. |
| `get_settings` | — | Returns `SettingsView` = the persisted `Settings` plus `jev_key_saved: bool`, `jev_env_override: bool` and `suggested_roots: string[]` (existing Documents/Desktop/Downloads). |
| `save_settings` | `(settings: Settings)` | Persists and applies immediately: Jev via `engine.set_jev`; roots and max file size apply on the next indexing run. Returns `SettingsView`. |
| `set_jev_key` | `(key: Option<String>)` | Stores the trimmed non-empty key in the OS credential store, or deletes it when `null`, then re-applies Jev. Returns `SettingsView`. Never written to `config.json` or logs. |
| `pick_folder` | — | `tauri-plugin-dialog` folder picker; returns `Option<String>` (window hide-on-blur is suppressed while it is open). |
| `start_index` | — | Background indexing of `settings.roots` at `settings.max_file_mb`; errors if a run is active or there are no roots. |
| `cancel_index` | — | Requests cancellation; the build stops at the next file and keeps the partial index (`BuildStats.cancelled = true`). |
| `status` | — | `{ready, roots, files, jev, hotkey, error, model_loaded, theme, indexing}` (the `root` field is replaced by `roots`); `hotkey` is the constant `Ctrl+Shift+Space`. |
| `open_path` | `(path: String, reveal: bool)` | Opens with the default app, or reveals in the file manager, then hides the window. |
| `hide_window` | — | Hides the `main` webview window. |

**Index progress event.** `start_index` emits the event `"index-progress"` at
most 4×/s with payload `{ state: "running"|"done"|"cancelled"|"error", done,
total, current, filesIndexed, filesReused, elapsedMs, message }`. Every 200
embedded files the partial index is saved and swapped into the engine, so
search works during a long run; a later run reuses those files and resumes.

### Settings (`config.json` in the app data dir)

`Settings` is serde with every field `#[serde(default)]` (unknown keys such as a
legacy `gpu` from an older `config.json` are ignored); the legacy
`{"root": "..."}` shape migrates to `roots: [root]`:

```json
{ "roots": ["C:\\Users\\me\\Documents"], "theme": "blue", "jev_enabled": false, "jev_privacy": "a",
  "max_file_mb": 10, "index_speed": "background" }
```

- `theme` ∈ `blue` | `violet` | `green` | `orange` (default `blue`); the theme
  sets accent **and** text colours.
- `index_speed` ∈ `background` (2 threads) | `fast` (all cores).
- `max_file_mb` — the `Scope` size cap for the next indexing run (default 10;
  larger files are hidden from semantic, grep and glob results everywhere).
- `jev_enabled`, `jev_privacy` — Jev switch and privacy level (`a`/`b`/`c`).

**Jev key storage.** The key is held in the Windows Credential Manager through
the `keyring` crate (v3, feature `windows-native`), service `"saan"`, user
`"jev-api-key"` — never in `config.json` or logs. `JevClient::from_env()` still
wins when `JEV_API_KEY` + `SAAN_JEV` are set; the CLI reads only the
environment.

App state is `AppState { engine: RwLock<Option<Engine>>, error: RwLock<Option<String>> }`.
The app is registered with `tauri-plugin-single-instance` (v2): launching
`saan-app.exe` again — including the `saan` CLI with no subcommand — hands the
`SAAN_SHOW` request to the running instance, which shows and focuses its window,
instead of starting a second process.

On startup the app registers the global shortcut `Ctrl+Shift+Space`; pressing it
toggles the window. If `SAAN_ROOT` is set it becomes the single root
(`roots = [SAAN_ROOT]`) and is (re)indexed first, otherwise the saved index
loads. The engine is constructed **without** loading
the model; it loads on the first semantic query, and the app drops it again with
`Engine::release_if_idle` after `SAAN_IDLE_UNLOAD_SECS` (default 300) seconds
without a semantic query, so an idle
launcher gives the ~197 MB back. The window hides on focus loss, and
`SAAN_SHOW` makes it visible at startup, after the first page load finishes
(showing earlier let WebView2 start-up hand focus back to the terminal, and the
window then hid itself on blur). Window config
(`src-tauri/tauri.conf.json`): label `main`, 720×560, undecorated, always on
top, centered, not resizable, skipped from the taskbar, initially hidden.

### Frontend (`index.html`, `src/main.ts`, `src/style.css`)

A single `#launcher` view: mode badge, query input, results listbox, folder
setup form and status footer. It calls the Tauri commands via
`@tauri-apps/api/core`'s `invoke`. Searches are debounced 40 ms and guarded by a
sequence number so a stale response cannot overwrite a newer one. `↑`/`↓` move
the selection, `Enter` opens, `Ctrl+Enter` reveals, `Escape` hides the window
(settings first, if open). Status is refreshed on window focus (and on a timer
while visible). Each result row also renders the hit's metadata — `size` (bytes),
`modified` (Unix seconds) and `ext` — so files that share a name are easy to
tell apart.

**Settings view.** A gear button in the search bar (or `Ctrl+,`) swaps the
results list for the settings view; `Esc` closes settings before hiding the
window. Sections: Appearance (four theme swatches), Folders (list with remove,
"Add folder…" via `pick_folder`, one-click add of `suggested_roots`, max file
size MB, index speed), Index (Start/Cancel, progress bar, done/total, ETA and
current file via `listen("index-progress")`), Jev (password field with
Save/Remove and "key saved" state, enable toggle, privacy A/B/C with one-line
descriptions and the env-override notice). Themes are `<html data-theme="blue|violet|green|orange">`,
setting `--bg`, `--panel`, `--line`, `--text`, `--dim` and `--accent` so text
and accent both follow the theme.

## Query data flow

`Engine::search(input, k)` in `crates/core/src/engine.rs`:

1. **Local route.** `local_route(input)` returns a `Route { mode, query,
   confidence, source }`.
2. **Optional Jev route.** Only when `route.confidence < CONFIDENT` (0.75) *and*
   a `JevClient` exists: one `POST /v1/systemone` asking for the mode. Any mode
   (including the same one) sets `source = Jev`; if the returned mode differs it
   is adopted, and when it is `grep` the raw input is `regex::escape`d so a
   plain string is safe as a regex.
3. **Dispatch.**
   - `semantic` → `Embedder::embed_query` then `Index::search` (top-k files by
     best-chunk cosine). The embedder is loaded on first use (cloned `Arc`
     outside the lock), so grep/glob searches never touch it.
   - `grep` → `grep::grep` over `index.scope()` with `GREP_HIT_LIMIT = 500`,
     one row per file (first matching line), `score = 1.0`, `line` set.
   - `glob` → `glob::glob` over `index.scope()`, `score = 1.0`, empty snippet.
   - Every hit also carries `size` (bytes), `modified` (Unix seconds, 0 when
     unknown) and `ext` (lowercase, no dot): semantic hits read them from
     `Index.files[i].size`/`mtime`, grep/glob hits from `std::fs::metadata`.
4. **Fallback to semantic.** If a *guessed* exact search (mode ≠ `semantic`, and
   `source != Explicit`, i.e. the user did not type a prefix) returns no hits,
   the route is replaced with a semantic search over the raw trimmed input.
5. **Same-name marking.** `mark_same_names` sets `same_name = true` on every hit
   whose lower-cased file name is shared with another hit in the response, so
   the UI can badge them.
6. **Optional Jev pick** (only `mode == semantic`, ≥ 2 hits, and a client):
   ambiguous when the top-two score margin `< PICK_MARGIN (0.02)` or any of the
   top `PICK_CANDIDATES (5)` hits has `same_name`. The top 5 are offered to
   `JevClient::pick`, whose `pick_request` returns `None` at privacy level `a`
   (so level `a` makes no pick call). A successful pick is moved to index 0.
7. Returns `SearchResponse { route, hits, jev_calls, elapsed_ms }`.

```mermaid
flowchart TD
  UI["Frontend index.html + src/main.ts"] -->|invoke| TC["Tauri commands main.rs"]
  CLI["saan CLI main.rs"] --> ENG
  TC --> ENG["Engine::search engine.rs"]
  ENG --> LR["local_route router.rs"]
  LR -->|confidence below CONFIDENT| JEV["JevClient jev.rs POST /v1/systemone"]
  ENG --> SEM["semantic: Embedder + Index::search"]
  ENG --> GR["grep.rs"]
  ENG --> GL["glob.rs"]
  SEM --> EMB["Embedder embed.rs EmbeddingGemma q4 ONNX"]
  SEM --> IDX["Index index.rs"]
  IDX --> EX["extract.rs"]
  IDX --> CH["chunk.rs"]
  JEV --> PICK["pick top candidate (privacy b/c)"]
  PICK --> ENG
```

## Index format

Two files, written by `Index::save` and read by `Index::load`:

- **`meta.json`** — `{ version: 2, roots: [...], max_file_bytes, dim, files:
  [{ root, rel, size, mtime }], chunks: [{ file, preview }] }`. `roots` are the
  scope's absolute root folders and `root` on a file entry is its index into
  that list; `rel` is root-relative with forward slashes; `size` is bytes and
  `mtime` is seconds since the Unix epoch; `preview` is the chunk text with
  whitespace collapsed, capped at `PREVIEW_CHARS = 240`; each chunk refers to
  its file by index. `FORMAT_VERSION = 2`: a version-1 index fails to load and
  the caller rebuilds.
- **`vectors.f32`** — row-major little-endian `f32`, one L2-normalised row of
  `dim` values per chunk.

Only content files (`is_content_file`: PDF plus a text/doc/code allow-list) are
stored in the index; every other file remains glob/grep-able because those walk
the disk through `Scope`. `load` rejects an unsupported `version` and a
vector-count mismatch (`chunks × dim`). Search computes each row's dot product
against the normalised query (so dot product = cosine), keeps the best chunk
per file, sorts descending and truncates to `k`.

### Scope (`crates/core/src/scope.rs`)

Indexing, grep and glob share one walk:

- `Scope::single(root)` (default cap `DEFAULT_MAX_FILE_BYTES = 10 MiB`) or
  `Scope::new(roots, max_file_bytes)`; the CLI takes `--max-file-mb`, the app
  `settings.max_file_mb`.
- `Scope::files()` lists every visible file under every root, sorted by
  `(root, rel)`, applying `.gitignore`/`.ignore`, hidden-file rules, `SKIP_DIRS`
  (matched on the directory name, case-insensitively) and the size cap: files
  larger than `max_file_bytes` never appear in semantic, grep or glob results.
- `ScopedFile { root, path, rel, size, mtime }`; `Scope::display_rel` renders
  `rel` unchanged for a single root and `<label>/<rel>` for several, the label
  being the root's last path component (or the drive, e.g. `C:`, for a drive
  root). `GrepHit.rel` and `GlobHit.rel` are display rels.

### Incremental reuse

`Index::build(&scope, embedder, previous, &BuildOptions { checkpoint_every },
on_event)`:

- Walks `scope.files()`; a previous entry is reused when its **absolute path**,
  `size` and `mtime` all match, so a rerun — or a resumed run after cancel —
  copies chunks and vectors instead of re-embedding (`files_reused`). Changed
  or new files are re-extracted; only content files are embedded.
- `BuildEvent::File { done, total, rel }` reports progress (`total` = files to
  (re)embed, `rel` = display path); `BuildEvent::Checkpoint(&Index)` fires
  every `checkpoint_every` embedded files (`0` = never — the app saves
  explicitly every 200 files instead). Returning `false` from `on_event`
  cancels: `build` returns the partial index of reused plus already-embedded
  files with `BuildStats.cancelled = true`.
- Embedding is batched `EMBED_BATCH = 8` chunks at a time; files longer than
  `MAX_CHUNKS_PER_FILE = 8` chunks embed only the first 8 (~10 KB). Embedding
  costs roughly 0.5 s per chunk on a laptop CPU, so this cap is the main lever on
  indexing time. On a real 276-file Documents + Desktop sample it keeps 69% of
  the chunks a 64-chunk cap embedded.
- `BuildStats` reports `files_seen`, `files_indexed`, `files_reused`,
  `chunks`, `cancelled`.

Reuse is thus keyed on **absolute path + size + mtime**, not content hashing.

## Embedding

- Model: **EmbeddingGemma-300m**, 4-bit ONNX (`onnx/model_q4.onnx` plus
  `onnx/model_q4.onnx_data`, constant `MODEL_FILE`), tokenizer and config from the public repo
  `onnx-community/embeddinggemma-300m-ONNX`, stored under
  `models/embeddinggemma-300m` (name `MODEL_DIR_NAME`).
- **Model license:** the app code is Apache-2.0, but these weights (from
  `onnx-community/embeddinggemma-300m-ONNX`, derived from
  `google/embeddinggemma-300m`, fetched by `saan fetch-model`) are governed by
  Google's [Gemma Terms of Use](https://ai.google.dev/gemma/terms), are not
  covered by this repo's license, and are not redistributed in the repo.
- Location resolved by `find_model_dir`: `$SAAN_MODEL_DIR`, else `models/<name>`
  under the current dir or any ancestor of the current dir / executable,
  requiring `tokenizer.json`.
- Session: ONNX Runtime with `GraphOptimizationLevel::Level3` and
  `intra_threads = $SAAN_THREADS` or `min(available_parallelism, 8)` (4 if unknown). Model
  dimension is probed with `embed_query("probe")`.
- Execution provider: `EmbedOptions { threads: Option<usize> }` —
  `Embedder::load_with(dir, opts)` runs on the **CPU** execution provider; no
  GPU/DirectML registration exists (spec R15 records why: the DirectML path
  measured p95 836–1072 ms vs 76–80 ms CPU). `Embedder::load(dir)` is
  `load_with(dir, EmbedOptions::default())`. The engine's `set_embed_options`
  unloads the current embedder when the options change, so the next query
  reloads with them.
- Prompts: documents are `doc_prompt(title, text)` =
  `title: {title} | text: {text}` where the title is `"{rel} ({file name})"`;
  queries are prefixed with `task: search result | query: `.
- Token caps: `MAX_DOC_TOKENS = 512`, `MAX_QUERY_TOKENS = 128`; the output
  `sentence_embedding` is L2-normalised per row.
- Chunks: ~1200 chars with 200 chars overlap (`chunk.rs`), so a chunk rarely
  exceeds the doc token cap.

## Jev privacy

Jev (TypeSafe AI System One) is opt-in and off by default. The API key comes
from `JEV_API_KEY` (`JevClient::from_env()`, unchanged — it also needs
`SAAN_JEV` to be `on`/`1`/`true`, and when set it overrides the app's saved
settings) **or** from the OS credential store: the settings panel saves it with
the `keyring` crate (v3, feature `windows-native`), service `"saan"`, user
`"jev-api-key"`, and hands it to `JevClient::new(key, privacy)` — never from a
file, and never written to `config.json` or logs. Requests go to
`POST {base}/v1/systemone` with `Authorization: Bearer <key>`, a 2500 ms global
timeout, and model `SAAN_JEV_MODEL` (default `jev-latest`).

| Level | Env value | Routing request | Candidate pick request |
|---|---|---|---|
| `a` (default) | `a` / `query` | query text | never sent |
| `b` | `b` / `paths` | query text | query + candidate relative paths |
| `c` | `c` / `snippets` | query text | query + candidate relative paths + snippets capped at `SNIPPET_CHARS = 160` |

Absolute paths, file contents beyond the snippet, and index data are never sent.
The route request body contains only the query at every level. The settings
panel offers the same three levels (`jev_privacy`, values `a`/`b`/`c`);
`SAAN_JEV_PRIVACY` applies when the environment path is active.

## Distribution and footprint

`saan` ships as two executables — `saan.exe` (CLI) and `saan-app.exe` (Tauri app)
— plus the model folder. The Windows installer (`scripts/install.ps1`) puts both
in `%LOCALAPPDATA%\saan\bin` and the model in
`%LOCALAPPDATA%\saan\models\embeddinggemma-300m`; because that model folder is a
`models/` ancestor of `bin`, `find_model_dir` resolves it without any environment
variable. saan embeds on the **CPU execution provider only** — on an RTX 4050
Laptop + i5-13420H the DirectML path measured p95 836–1072 ms vs 76–80 ms CPU
(uncached `saan bench fixtures/eval.json`), so the GPU option was removed.

The ~197 MB model is not resident by default: `Engine::new` takes a directory and
loads the `Embedder` lazily on the first semantic query, so an idle launcher is
just the Tauri process (+ WebView2). `SAAN_IDLE_UNLOAD_SECS` (default 300) makes
the app drop the model again when no semantic query has run for that long.

## Environment variables

| Variable | Read by | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| `SAAN_MODEL_DIR` | `embed::find_model_dir`, CLI `fetch-model` | Model folder (also the download destination). |
| `SAAN_INDEX_DIR` | CLI `index_dir` | Index folder when `--index` is not given. |
| `SAAN_THREADS` | `Embedder::load_with` | ONNX Runtime intra-op threads (default `min(cores, 8)`). |
| `SAAN_ROOT` | Tauri `startup` | Root folder to (re)index at launch: `roots = [SAAN_ROOT]`. |
| `SAAN_SHOW` | Tauri `setup` / `on_page_load` | Show the window once the page has loaded (any value). The CLI sets `SAAN_SHOW=1` when it spawns the app. |
| `SAAN_APP` | CLI (no subcommand) | Path to the desktop app binary; default is `saan-app[.exe]` next to the running `saan` executable. |
| `SAAN_IDLE_UNLOAD_SECS` | Tauri idle unload | Seconds without a semantic query, with the window hidden, before the app drops the model (default 300; checked every 30 s). |
| `SAAN_JEV` | `JevClient::from_env` | Enables Jev when `on`, `1` or `true`. |
| `JEV_API_KEY` | `JevClient::from_env` | Bearer token for the environment path (required with `SAAN_JEV`); when set it overrides the key saved in the Windows Credential Manager. The key is never read from a file. |
| `SAAN_JEV_PRIVACY` | `JevClient::from_env` | `a`/`query` (default), `b`/`paths`, `c`/`snippets`; overrides the settings privacy level when the env path is active. |
| `SAAN_JEV_URL` | `JevClient::from_env` | API base URL (default `https://api.typesafe.ai`); trailing `/` trimmed. |
| `SAAN_JEV_MODEL` | `JevClient::from_env` | Model name (default `jev-latest`). |

